{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/834501-searching-for-armor-houserules","id":834501,"title":"Searching for armor houserules","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-21T11:05:45-08:00","id":834501,"title":"Searching for armor houserules","content":"I've been looking at the armor rules lately, since a DA campain may be starting soon, and I am quite dissatisfied with the way armor is portayed in the core books.<br /> Currently, me and my group are looking to devellop a houserule regarding this, finding a way to make armor work in our games.<br /> <br /> Are there any houserules for armor the rest of you deploy?<br /> How much armor dice do you give out, how do you handle weight-penaltys, what about armor-piercing weapons and such?<br /> I'd be thankfull for any input, you might have for me and my crew. ;-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T12:23:55-08:00","id":834560,"title":"","content":"Can you say what problems you have with the existing rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T13:09:59-08:00","id":834594,"title":"","content":"At the moment armor is unrealistically ineffective and the way, that the dex penaltys are set up, leads to there being a &quot;best&quot; armor out of no concernable reason.<br /> <br /> Dex is by far the most important of the physical Attributes. Trading 3 Dex for 5 Armor is a bad deal, no matter how you slice it.<br /> So wearing heavy armor is more of a penalty than a bonus, in a way.<br /> The only two armors, that actually work in your favor are extremly light ones (one armor dice, no penaltys) and composite ones (3 armor dice, 1 dex penalty).<br /> So the way its written at the moment, you ether take &quot;sturdy clothing&quot; if you don't really need armor but don't mind the extra dice, or take composite armor, when armor is actually needed for the char.<br /> I'd like for the other kinds of armor to be more viable, having a reason to be worn exept simply for style.<br /> <br /> Also, armor seems surprisingly weak in actually stopping damage.<br /> Still trying to find a balance, but 1-5 extra dice on absorbing damage seems laughable litte when compared to how much protection one would expect from being armored up quite some bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T13:24:09-08:00","id":834602,"title":"","content":"Not my idea, but I played in a game where armor added a number of Health Levels equal to its rating as well as the usual way it works. It's not perfect, but it might be something to consider. <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you don't use an Oxford comma, I feel bad for you, son,<br /> 'Cuz I got ninety-nine problems, but clarity ain't one.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing","name":"nothing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar408_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T13:37:23-08:00","id":834610,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/408-nothing\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar408_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"408\" data-vbnamecard=\"408\">nothing</a> thanks for the input. This is an interesting idea, though I don't think we will use that one. Still, I'll ad it to the list of possible solutions. Thank you :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T15:03:17-08:00","id":834645,"title":"","content":"The M20 armor rules are probably one of the better sets for your concerns just using the RAW. The Dex penalties are lower, and vaguer (it is not phrased as all Dex dice-pools, so you can exercise more discretion about it), shields have separate stats that stack with armors (Riot armor is 4/-2, and a riot shield is 5/-1 vs. firearms, so you're at 9 soak dice against guns with a -3 penalty, and hand-to-hand attacks suffer a +2 difficulty against you; all with the caveat that shields don't work against flank or surprise attacks).<br /> <br /> Also remember that specified targets to avoid armor are going to be a lot easier against many lighter armors since they don't have full body protection or helmets.<br /> <br /> If you're looking for more options:<br /> <br /> Give armors tags (such as ballistic, slashing, stab) to reflect being designed for different situations. Light armors like reinforced clothing will have no or one of these, while heavier armors will usually have more of them and/or broader ones. Whenever the tag applies, it reduces lethal damage <i>dealt</i> to bashing damage up to the armors rating. So a person wearing a Kevlar vest that's shot for 4 damage post-soak, takes 1 lethal and 3 bashing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T23:46:08-08:00","id":834863,"title":"","content":"There are expanded armor rules in VtM Revised Storytellers Companion. It has different soak stats for bullets, slashing, piercing etc. Maybe you want to take a look at those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T11:00:48-08:00","id":835180,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Thanks for your ideas, they seem very very intersting. Those are definetly on the list for consideration.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar392_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"392\" data-vbnamecard=\"392\">Cadmiumcadamium</a> I will check them out right away, thanks for the tip. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T22:40:59-08:00","id":837394,"title":"","content":"Important thing to remember is that the Dex penalty only applies to non-attack rolls. Armor doesn't inhibit your ability to swing a sword or to shoot a gun. So basically dodging is kinda the only thing gimped.<br /> <br /> A house rule that does tend to work is having the armor give autosoak. Makes the guy in Kelvar suddenly that much more dangerous. Obviously should use damage rules for armor in one form or another.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T00:06:03-08:00","id":839001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>theoutlander523</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/834501-searching-for-armor-houserules?p=837394#post837394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Important thing to remember is that the Dex penalty only applies to non-attack rolls. Armor doesn't inhibit your ability to swing a sword or to shoot a gun. So basically dodging is kinda the only thing gimped.<br /> <br /> A house rule that does tend to work is having the armor give autosoak. Makes the guy in Kelvar suddenly that much more dangerous. Obviously should use damage rules for armor in one form or another.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where did you get this from? I have never come across a rule that specifically states that attack rolls are excluded from the dicepool penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-29T00:49:03-08:00","id":839012,"title":"","content":"I don't recall specifically which books, but I'm pretty sure some of them have done that (I'm thinking DA). It's something that's seen a lot of variation across game lines and editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T13:18:01-08:00","id":840140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, armor also subtracts a number of dice from dice pools related to bodily coordination and agility (most Dexterity-based dice pools). This is reflected in the penalty listing. </div> </div> </div>V20 book has it stated. If you honestly think armor would reduce dice pools for swinging a sword or using a gun, then I suggest you go to Youtube and watch armored combat fights. As for guns, our military wouldn't use it ever if it made shooting a gun harder. The writers also stated this some where in the forums a long while back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1VN49Y7tH2ZV0l7Hx65RWX1ez-Q9Lst-8ZTyTJeCTpxM/\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerer 20th</a> homebrew and my update to <a href=\"http://immortalthegathering.blogspot.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Highlander: the Gathering</a> for 20th Anniversary edition.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2414-theoutlander523","name":"theoutlander523","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-11T04:30:46-08:00","id":845557,"title":"","content":"In the end it's what you want in your game. I would say armor's dexterity penalty doesn't apply to attacks unless those attacks somehow included flips or some extreme.movement before hand to make the attack. As for dodge it does make sense since an armored character is less likely to attempt to dodge the more armor he is wearing, both from the penalty and also the confidence of not needing to dodge as well. <br /> <br /> I would consider for every 2 points of armor one could get an automatic soak instead of rolling 2 of their armor dice. <br /> <br /> Armor adding extra health levels doesn't fit to well. Unless you are going to really play with armor damaged and damaged often that doesn't work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11414-kilcannon","name":"Kilcannon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}